out it.\n\nIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n\n\n## B09.1\n\n**Check:** Outbound traffic is default-deny, with a destination allowlist enforced at a proxy, gateway, or network policy.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find egress rules (NetworkPolicy egress, Cilium FQDN, proxy ACLs, cloud firewall). 2) Check outbound is default deny with a destination allowlist. 3) Answer no if egress allows `0.0.0.0/0` or broad CIDRs, no egress rules exist, or the allowlist is only in app code the agent runs. Answer unknown if egress is set outside this repo.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Default-deny egress to the proxy is set but the destination allowlist lives in the platform proxy outside this repo\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## B09.2\n\n**Check:** Network policy blocks direct routes around the proxy or gateway, for both IPv4 and IPv6.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Check whether the proxy is enforced by network policy or only by `HTTP_PROXY`/`HTTPS_PROXY` env. 2) Check IPv6 egress rules. 3) Answer no if pods can reach the internet except via the proxy, the proxy is only an env var, `NO_PROXY` is broad, or IPv6 is not restricted.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** k8s/deployment.yaml:193 — \"ipBlock: { cidr: 10.60.12.0/28 }\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** NetworkPolicy blocks routes around the proxy\n\n`k8s/deployment.yaml` lines 181–195 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n 181              matchLabels: { k8s-app: kube-dns }\n 182        ports:\n 183          - { port: 53, protocol: UDP }\n 184          - { port: 53, protocol: TCP }\n 185      - to:\n 186          - namespaceSelector:\n 187              matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: platform }\n 188            podSelector:\n 189              matchLabels: { app: egress-proxy }\n 190        ports:\n 191          - { port: 3128, protocol: TCP }\n 192      - to:\n 193>         - ipBlock: { cidr: 10.60.12.0/28 }\n 19