{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdbUVeADDSBugB7dfFsa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `verdict.json` with an overall verdict of **failed**, because B09.3 fails.\n\n- **B09.1, unclear:** The NetworkPolicy is default-deny. It allows only DNS, the platform egress proxy on port 3128, and one IPv4 /28 on port 443. The destination allowlist itself sits in the platform proxy, which isn't in this repo.\n- **B09.2, holds:** The NetworkPolicy forces traffic through the proxy rather than relying on the `HTTPS_PROXY` env var. There is no IPv6 or `0.0.0.0/0` egress rule, so IPv6 is denied by default.\n- **B09.3, fails:** `agent/src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83` calls `createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(header.jku))`. The `jku` value comes from the peer's attestation header and is fetched before the signature is verified. The app has no host allowlist, resolved-IP check, or metadata/loopback block, and the fetch calls follow redirects by default. Any protection would have to come from the external proxy.\n- **B09.4, unclear:** Per-resource and tenant limits would live in the proxy. The comment at `agent/k8s/deployment.yaml:160` says it allows \"AWS service endpoints\" generally, with no visible limit on which resources.\n- **B09.5, unclear:** Logging of blocked requests and alert routing to a named operator are not in this repo.\n\nFor `violates` I copied \"Cover redirects, DNS changes and rebinding, IPv4 and IPv6, and cloud metadata or loopback addresses where they apply\" from the requirement.\n\nI did not run anything or edit the agent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1800,"cache_read_input_tokens":21322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1800},"output_tokens":566,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"d